        "content": "<strong> The SM58 is the most popular vocal microphone in the world, and it's the SM57's vocal-focused sibling. </strong>It shares the same tank-like dynamic capsule, but the ball grille doubles as a built-in pop filter and wind shield, and the presence boost around 5 kHz helps vocals cut through a loud live mix or a dense recording. The tight cardioid pattern rejects room noise, so it's forgiving in an untreated home office or bedroom studio â€” no acoustic treatment required. On a live stage it's the undisputed standard, and in front of a computer it handles spoken word, singing and podcasting with a warm, present, honest tone. If you need one mic that does vocals anywhere, the SM58 is the safest you can spend.\n<p><strong>Pair it with:</strong> the SM58 ships without cable or stand, so add <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B001LNN2EQ?tag=topmusicg-20\" rel=\"nofollow sponsored\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"guide-link-btn\">a Mogami Gold Studio XLR cable</a> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0006PQOF4?tag=topmusicg-20\" rel=\"nofollow sponsored\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"guide-link-btn\">a un soporte K&M 210/2</a> The ball grille is already a built-in pop filter and wind shield, so you're set for stage vocals the moment it's plugged in.</p>",
